PREPROCESSING STEPS

1. Excel: grouped parents' qualification codes
   Formula applied to Mother qualification (column I) and Father qualification (column J),
   then pasted as values over the original codes:
   =IF(ISNUMBER(MATCH(I2,{2,3,4,5,6,40,41,42,43,44},0)),"Higher",
    IF(ISNUMBER(MATCH(I2,{1,9,10,12,13,14,18,20,22,25,27,31,33,39},0)),"Secondary",
    IF(ISNUMBER(MATCH(I2,{11,19,26,29,30,35,36,37,38},0)),"Basic",
    IF(I2=34,"Unknown","CHECK"))))
   Result: Basic / Secondary / Higher / Unknown (no "CHECK" values left)

2. Excel: grouped parents' occupation codes
   Mother occupation (column K) and Father occupation (column L):
   Result: High-skilled / Clerical/service / Manual skilled / Low-skilled / Other/unknown

3. Excel: binary target (Dropout + Enrolled -> Not on time)
   Target (column AK):
   [paste target formula]
   Result: Graduate 2209 / Not on time 2215 -> saved as data_all.csv

4. Weka: removed Nationality and 2nd semester columns
   weka.filters.unsupervised.attribute.Remove -R 8,30-33
   weka.filters.unsupervised.attribute.Remove -R 27-28
   - Nationality: highly correlated with International (r = 0.91), kept International
   - 2nd semester (6 columns): not available at the time of prediction in either stage

5. Weka: numeric to nominal
   weka.filters.unsupervised.attribute.NumericToNominal -R 1,2,4,5,6,8-11,13-18,20
   Kept numeric: application order, previous qualification grade, admission grade,
   age at enrollment, 1st semester curricular units, unemployment rate, inflation rate, GDP

6. Weka: stratified 80/20 split, Stage 2 (includes 1st semester, 30 attributes)
   weka.filters.supervised.instance.StratifiedRemoveFolds -S 0 -N 5 -F 1      -> test_stage2.arff  (885: 443 / 442)
   weka.filters.supervised.instance.StratifiedRemoveFolds -S 0 -V -N 5 -F 1   -> train_stage2.arff (3539: 1772 / 1767)

7. Weka: stratified 80/20 split, Stage 1 (no semester data, 24 attributes)
   Starting again from the data after step 5, removed 1st semester columns:
   weka.filters.unsupervised.attribute.Remove -R 21-26
   weka.filters.supervised.instance.StratifiedRemoveFolds -S 0 -N 5 -F 1      -> test_stage1.arff  (885: 443 / 442)
   weka.filters.supervised.instance.StratifiedRemoveFolds -S 0 -V -N 5 -F 1   -> train_stage1.arff (3539: 1772 / 1767)

   Same seed (0) in both stages, so Stage 1 and Stage 2 use exactly the same
   test students. All transformations were applied before splitting, so train
   and test files have identical headers.
